# Vercel Web Analytics Integration

Successfully implemented Vercel Web Analytics for the Next.js App Router project.

## Changes Made:

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` version 1.6.1 using pnpm
- Updated `package.json` to include the new dependency
- Generated `pnpm-lock.yaml` to lock dependency versions

### 2. Analytics Integration
Modified: `app/layout.tsx`
- Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next"`
- Added `<Analytics />` component inside the `<body>` tag, after the `{children}` component
- Placement follows best practices for App Router projects

## Implementation Details:

The Analytics component was added to the root layout file (`app/layout.tsx`) which is the correct approach for Next.js App Router projects. The component is placed at the end of the body tag to ensure it loads after the main application content, which is optimal for performance.

## Verification:

✓ Build completed successfully with no errors
✓ TypeScript compilation passed
✓ All routes generated correctly (11 static pages)
✓ Linter found no new errors (pre-existing warnings remain unchanged)

## Files Modified:
- `app/layout.tsx` - Added Analytics import and component
- `package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics dependency
- `pnpm-lock.yaml` - Generated lockfile for new dependency (new file)

The implementation preserves all existing code structure and only adds the necessary changes for Vercel Web Analytics integration.
